Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 02:25:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the member directory: user search and public profiles

The website's community search box could only search the companions a
signed-in member already has (GET /api/companions), so typing a name
never found anybody new - and a profile URL (/profile?id=<20-digit uid>)
that was not a companion already could not be resolved at all. The guest
tour, which carries a seeded directory of every traveler, finds and opens
anybody. This is the API side of that parity:

* GET /api/users/search?query=&limit= - finds Active members by first /
  last / full name (and city, country, profession), name hits ranked
  first. The signed-in member, members who switched off their search
  visibility and members blocked in either direction are never returned.
  Every hit answers its companionship status, isFollowing and mutual
  companions count, so the search drop-down can offer Connect / Request
  Sent / Connected and Follow / Following straight away.

* GET /api/users/{id} and GET /api/users/uid/{uniqueId} - any member's
  public profile as the same CompanionDto the companions endpoints answer
  (relationship status, mutuals, About-me JSON, cover URL), so the
  website can open a stranger's profile exactly like the guest tour.
  Privacy: a non-public profile answers 403; WhoCanVisitProfile
  (companions / none) trims the answer to the identity cards of a locked
  profile; a locked profile hides its About-me content from
  non-companions; Pending accounts are never answered to other members.

* CompanionDto gains IsFollowing, answered by the companions endpoints as
  well, so the website's follow buttons agree with the database.

README documents the directory endpoints.
