+- **Member directory — search and public profiles (`UsersController`).** The community
+  search box must find *any* member, not only the companions a signed-in traveler
+  already has, and a profile URL (`/profile?id=<20-digit uid>`) must open the real
+  profile of the member it points at. Three endpoints close that gap:
+  - `GET /api/users/search?query=&limit=` matches Active members by first / last / full
+    name (and city, country, profession), ranking name hits first. The signed-in member,
+    members who switched off `UserSettings.SearchVisibility` and members blocked in
+    either direction are never returned. Each hit carries its companionship `status`,
+    `isFollowing` and `mutualCompanionsCount`, so the search drop-down can offer
+    Connect / Request Sent / Connected and Follow / Following directly.
+  - `GET /api/users/{id}` and `GET /api/users/uid/{uniqueId}` answer the same
+    `CompanionDto` the companions endpoints use (relationship status, mutuals, About-me
+    JSON, cover URL), so the website opens any member's profile exactly like the guest
+    tour does. Privacy: a non-public profile answers 403; `WhoCanVisitProfile`
+    ("companions" / "none") trims the answer to the identity cards of a locked profile;
+    a locked profile hides its About-me content from non-companions. Pending (not yet
+    registered) accounts are never answered to other members.
+  - `CompanionDto.IsFollowing` is now answered by the companions endpoints too, so the
+    website's follow buttons agree with the database.
+  - Name search is fast on big member tables with the trigram indexes of
+    `neverbeen-database-user-search.patch` (optional — ILIKE works without them).
